<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mozambique</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mozambique is a country on the coast of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. The Portuguese established trading posts on its coast from the early sixteenth century and pushed inland along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a>, interacting with and undermining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a>. Mozambique remained a Portuguese colony until independence in 1975 after a long war, one of the last parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mozambique.jpg" alt="Mozambique" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FRELIMO · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mozambique.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
